2045. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 15200779
T1  - Use and abuse of centrally-acting drugs: Stimulants and hallucinogens
A1  - Morris R.W. 
Y1  - 1984//
N2  - Goals: To review current therapeutic applications of stimulants and hallucinogens. To introduce and/or update knowledge about to-day's major street drug problems with stimulants and hallucinogens. To make pharmacists more aware of the roles they can play in street drug problems. To encourage pharmacists to get involved in finding and implementing solutions to street drug problems. Objectives: To review therapeutic applications of stimulants and hallucinogens. To familiarize the pharmacist with the more common types of illicit stimulants and hallucinogens. To identify unusual street drug problems and fads. To characterize physical, psychological and behavioral responses associated with the use, misuse and abuse of stimulants and hallucinogens. To provide enough street information about stimulants and hallucinogens so as to increase the self-confidence of the readers in their personal street drug knowledge. On the basis of an increased self-confidence in their drug knowledge, to encourage the readers to be more active in community drug programs.
