2051. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 15181992
T1  - The hallucinogens and the inhalants
A1  - Cohen S. 
Y1  - 1984//
N2  - Chronic use of inhalants can produce temporary or permanent organ dysfunction. In the 30 years since juvenile inhalant abuse was first noted in this country, it appears to have spread according to an epidemiologic model, that is, from a single person or small group to a vulnerable population, through peer contact. In certain ethnic groups, its use is widespread enough to be considered a serious public health problem. Control of the inhalant problem consists of making supplies more difficult to obtain, preventing new outbreaks, and treating individuals requiring medical help. It is in the area of prevention that any major breakthrough must come forth. Inhalant abuse is a relatively minor part of the greater problem of drug abuse.
