2058. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 13123685
T1  - Pharmacology of drugs of abuse
T3  - ZUR PHARMAKOLOGIE VON RAUSCHMITTELN UND SUCHTERREGENDEN DROGEN
A1  - Forth W. 
Y1  - 1983//
N2  - The pharmacological and toxicological effects of drugs of abuse have long been known and are well documented in man and animals. This knowledge is valuable not only in the treatment of acute drug intoxication but also in the management of the psychophysical symptoms of withdrawal. Nevertheless, even a detailed knowledge of the effects of these drugs does not throw much light on their most characteristic feature - their habit forming potential. This implies that explanations of the process of habit formation, which are based on physical dependence alone, continue to be unsatisfactory, as they take no account of the personal situation of the patient affected.
