ID  - 14013445
T1  - Drug addiction
A1  - Ceccaldi P.F. 
Y1  - 1983//
N2  - If it were possible to compile a list of the consequences classified in order of seriousness, society might perhaps consider that most forms of drug addiction are actually less dangerous than alcoholism or smoking (whose effects occur later or at any rate develop more slowly) because drug addiction affects limited groups of people who are already indulging in various forms of vice and have already more or less placed themselves outside society, whilst alcoholism and tobacco-addiction often seem to be better tolerated but have a tendency to spread in a more insidious fashion. This raises the whole question of which drugs are socially acceptable and which are not. We shall only be considering addiction to the socially unacceptable drugs
