2073. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 13246524
T1  - Two-photon photoionization detection of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons and drugs in a windowless flow cell
A1  - Voigtman E.
A1  - Winefordner J.D. 
Y1  - 1982//
N2  - A laser-excited windowless flow cell has been developed that has simultaneous detection capabilities by molecular fluorescence, photoacoustic effect, and two-photon photoionization processes. Factors of primary influence on the analytical performance of the photoionization mode have been evaluated with polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) as model compounds and a variety of drugs having diverse structures have been detected in the photoionization mode. A liquid phase photoionization chromatogram demonstrates the analytical merit of the technique.
