2080. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 12050639
T1  - Addiction and abuse of illegal drugs and solvents
T3  - SUCHT UND MISSBRAUCH VON ILLEGALEN DROGEN UND SCHNUFFELSTOFFEN
A1  - Haan J. 
Y1  - 1982//
N2  - The most commonly used illegal drugs are hallucinogens and psychostimulants such as hashish, marijuana, and cocaine, and the morphine derivative, heroin. These drugs not only induce acute symptoms such as dry mouth and conjunctival irritation, but can also be responsible for asthma, tachycardia, and severe nausea with vomiting. Chronic abuse induce personality changes, and psychosis is not infrequent. Special emergency measures are necessary in life-threatening situations where hospitalisation is unavoidable.
