T1  - Mechanism of action of psychotropic drugs
T3  - WIRKUNGSMECHANISMEN PSYCHOTROPER DROGEN
A1  - Binder M. 
Y1  - 1981//
N2  - Neurobiochemical mechanisms are described with reference to four examples; the analgetic, morphine (opiates); the tranquillizers of the benzodiazepine group; the hallucinogenic agent, lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD); and the active agent of hashish, DELTA1-tetrahydrocannabinol. In an introduction, the principles of electrical and chemical conduction of stimuli in the brain are listed, and possible sites of attack and mechanisms of action of the psychotropic drugs are discussed.
