T1  - Psychotomimetic agents: lysergide (LSD), psilocybine and mescaline
T3  - HALLUZINOGENE: LSD, PSILOCYBIN UND MESCALIN
A1  - Konzett H. 
Y1  - 1981//
N2  - LSD, psilocybin and mescaline following oral intake have an overwhelming effect on perception, sensitivity,personality and feeling for time in the sense of a model psychosis with euphoria but occasionally also dysphoric moodiness. The psychotoxicity of these agents is not inconsiderable. Experimental investigations indicate that they have a multiplicity of effects on the central nervous system.
