2105. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 12176347
T1  - Anaesthesia and drug addition; hallucinogenic drugs
T3  - ANESTESIA E TOSSICOMANIE: GLI ALLUCINOGENI
A1  - Peduto V.A.
A1  - Masini E.
A1  - Pieraccioli E.
A1  - Novelli G.P. 
Y1  - 1981//
N2  - In relation to the ever increasing diffusion of drug addiction, to the hypothetical interferences of the drugs of abuse with those of anaesthesia, and to the peculiar difficulties facing the anaesthetist with an addicted patient, we thought of topical interest to examine, from the anaesthesiologist's viewpoint, the questionable aspects of this social problem. In this review the hallucinogenic drugs (marihuana, LSD, phencyclidine, mescaline, psilocybin and psychotomimetic amphetamines) have been studied. More than four hundred citations are reported.
