2117. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 10162568
T1  - Abuse of the mushroom Panaeolus foenisecii
A1  - Cooles P. 
Y1  - 1980//
N2  - The mushroom commonly used for hallucinogenic purposes in the United Kingdom is Psilocybe semilanceata (the Liberty cap). The pharmacological effect of these mushrooms is said to be caused by 4-hydroxy-tryptamine derivatives (psilocybin and psilocin). The author describes here the ingestion, for its hallucinogenic properties, of a common mushroom, Panaeolus foenisecii, found in lawns and parkland, often around blocks of flats in Aberdeen.
