2138. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 9055211
T1  - Pharmacological aspects of drugs
A1  - Kutsch Lojenga J.C. 
Y1  - 1978//
N2  - The crucial subject of research into the pharmacology of addiction is naturally: where is the physiological-anatomical substrate on which the drug acts? It is easy to understand that in the search for an answer to this question, morphine has received most attention. Other important questions are: what led the addict to begin using a drug, and why has its use been continued? This short overview considers these questions with reference to morphine, CNS stimulants, hallucinogens, and cannabis.
