2148. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6200475
T1  - Treatment of chronic inflammatory and toxic metabolic liver damages with young drug addiction and alcoholics by Hepsan
T3  - BEHANDLUNG CHRONISCH ENTZUNDLICHER UND TOXISCH METABOLISCHER LEBERSCHADEN BEI JUGENDLICHEN DROGENABHANGIGEN UND ALKOHOLIKERN MIT HEPSAN
A1  - Nett H.H. 
Y1  - 1975//
N2  - In the years 1971-74 60 young men aged from 18 to 24 years were treated for chronic inflammatory and toxic metabolic diseases of the liver. They were classified as follows: drug addicts, 53.1%; alcoholics, 39.8%; ill after taking medicines, 5.0%. The therapy consisted of 2 to 3 intramuscular injections of 3000 gamma cyanocobalamin per week, for three weeks. At the same time and after cessation of the injections as long term treatment, 2 capsules 3 times a day for at least 3 months. The high quota of normalization of hepatogenic dysproteinaemias by the therapy is significant; it permits the conclusion that Hepsan has a direct favourable action on chronic intermittent and persisting forms of the course of drug hepatitis, and on alcoholic fatty hepatitis.
