2167. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 10227106
T1  - LSD, psychotogenic procedures, and brain neurohumors
A1  - Freedman D.X. 
Y1  - 1979//
N2  - The psychopharmacology of indoleamine and phenylethylamine hallucinogens is being explored, particularly with regard to the effects of these drugs on the metabolism of brain amines. The experiments are designed to elucidate the mechanisms accountable for amine-dependent and amine-mediated behavioral effects of psychotomimetics, the differences among the indoleamine hallucinogens and between the indoleamines and phenylethylamines, and the development of tolerance to the effects of these compounds. In addition, these studies are aimed at exploring basic mechanisms of central monoaminergic transmission.
