2171. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 10129216
T1  - An economical screen for phenethylamine-type hallucinogens: Mouse ear scratching
A1  - Yim G.K.W.
A1  - Prah T.E.
A1  - Pfister W.R. 
Y1  - 1979//
N2  - When evaluated with DOM isomers and a number of hallucinogenic and non-hallucinogenic agents, the mouse ear scratch response was found to be stereo-selective and capable of ranking the phenethylamine-type compounds in order of observed human potency. The test, however, was not sensitive to tryptamine-type hallucinogens such as LSD and psilocybin. However, because it is inexpensive, easy to score and requires a minimal amount of test compound, the mouse ear scratch response may still be useful as an initial predictive test for potential hallucinogenic activity of phenethylamines.
