2201. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 9126903
T1  - Drugs and Eros: Reflections on aphrodisiacs
A1  - Gawin F.H. 
Y1  - 1978//
N2  - Notions of aphrodisiacs have invariably focused towards sex emphasizing performance, drive and frequency, on increasing libido, and, in a relative sense, ignored the more qualitative distinctions of simple sexual pleasure. The present study seeks alleviation of this situation by extending the definition of 'aphrodisiac' to include an effect on subjective pleasure experienced in sexual activity, independent of changes in drive; and thus hopes to open new avenues of thought, research and application. It is concluded that a libido-oriented model of aphrodisiacs has left a potentially fruitful area of exploration untapped. Perhaps sexuality can be enhanced pharmacologically. Medical and societal morality and narrowness of outlook may have limited definition and exploration in the past. One hopes that an enlightened medical community has emerged such that this will not be the case in the future.
