N2  - This paper analyzes the possible interactions of a series of molecules of the phencyclidine family with a series of neurotransmitter receptors.One interesting difference between muscarinic antagonists resides in the fact that antagonists bind to the muscarinic receptor with a Hill coefficient of 1, e.g., without any indication of cooperativity, whereas agonists display a marked negative cooperativity of binding with Hill coefficients of 0.5-0.6. The Hill coefficient for 4Mt, n(H) = 0.9, suggests strongly that the molecule is an antagonist of the muscarinic receptor
