2212. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 9038696
T1  - Thin-layer chromatography for rapid identification of some hallucinogenic drugs
T3  - SCHNELLNACHWEIS VON RAUSCHGIFTEN MIT DER DUNNSCHICHT-CHROMATOGRAPHIE IM APOTHEKENLABORATORIUM
A1  - Stahl E.
A1  - Brombeer J. 
Y1  - 1978//
N2  - In the introduction, origin and abuse of the presently most often encountered plant drugs, such as cannabis and opium and their active ingredients, are discussed. Special attention is given to the heroin hits and their various adulterants as well as to the description of the safe proof of LSD traces in mushrooms and the detection of psilocybine and psilocine in Mexican hallucinogenic mushrooms. Reliable and proven thin-layer chromatographic procedures - easily applicable in every pharmacy laboratory - are given for fast and safe identification of some hallucinogenic drugs on the black market.
