T1  - Ethnological, chemical and toxicological features of hallucinogenic mushrooms
T3  - I FUNGHI ALLUCINOGENI. CONSIDERAZIONI ETNOLOGICHE E CHIMICO-TOSSICOLOGICHE
A1  - Marozzi E. 
Y1  - 1977//
N2  - The main hallucinogenic substances and the basic clinical and pharmacological effects of Amanita muscaria and Stropharia are described. The reasons for Watson's view that fly agaric may have been the 'Soma' of the Vedic books are also explained. The part by drugs among primitive peoples is compared with that observed in the modern world.
