ID  - 8169313
T1  - Hallucinogens in the United States: a diagnostic evaluation
A1  - Cleckner P.J. 
Y1  - 1977//
N2  - One may interpret the use of hallucinogens in the United States as a cultural response to stress conditions, the formal nature of which resembles anti-structural phenomena in other cultural settings. The experience was not productive for all participants, but for many it provided an important tool in facilitating creation of new models appropriate to resolution of existing conflicts. Rather than being merely an example of deviant and marginal behavior, it represented a social movement which continues in altered form among many splinter groups and which has had considerable impact on the dominant culture.
