2246. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 8058430
T1  - Emotional and cognitive structures and psychosis. New perspectives of the study of the hallucinatory experience with psychodysleptics
T3  - STRUCTURES AFFECTIVO COGNITIVES ET PSYCHOSES. NOUVELLES PERSPECTIVES DE L'ETUDE DE L'EXPERIENCE HALLUCINATOIRE AUX PSYCHODYSLEPTIQUES
A1  - Andreoli A. 
Y1  - 1976//
N2  - This paper compares classic experimental 'model psychosis' psychodysleptic induced and psychotic adverse reactions to psychodysleptic habitude or episodic use as clinically observed. Biochemical, neurophysiological and psychopathological background of psychodysleptic states and clinical data are discussed in an aim to investigate and explain interaction between cognitive and affective destructuration in the falling off of psychotic crises. A multidisciplinary approach provides new insight about destructuration processes in exogenous or endogenous psychoses and about mental development in the child.
