2256. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 7108362
T1  - Observations on the phenomenology of consciousness change
A1  - Zinberg N.E. 
Y1  - 1976//
N2  - This essay will consider the phenomenology of changes in consciousness colloquially known as 'high' states. The experimental section focuses solely on descriptive generalizations of opiate and psychedelic drug induced states. These particular high states have been selected for reasons of research strategy and because they are sufficiently prominent to justify emphasis on what has prevented us from progressing further in such studies.
