2277. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 7217299
T1  - The aminergic system of the CNS and the psychosomatic reaction (Greek)
A1  - Parashos A. 
Y1  - 1976//
N2  - In an effort to explain the manifestations of psychosomatic reactions the phenomenology of these entities is discussed in relation to the activities of the monoaminergic neuron systems of the CNS. These activities (noradrenergic, dopaminergic and 5 hydroxy tryptaminergic) are considered of primary importance in the emotional expression and its influences on the psychomotor behavior and neurovegetative control mechanisms of the body economy. There is strong evidence about the correlations of monoaminergic neuronic activities and the formulation of emotions, which has emerged through recent neurochemical investigations on Parkinson's syndrome and pharmacodynamic analysis of the modern psychoactive drugs. It is the author's opinion that neurochemical research might explain the pathomechanisms of psychosomatic reactions.
