2282. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6158492
T1  - In vitro action of psilocybin in lymphocyte cultures
A1  - Marquez Monter H.
A1  - Ruiz Ramirez E.
A1  - Carranza Acevedo J. 
Y1  - 1975//
N2  - This report describes in vitro studies of psilocybine (from hallucinogenic mushrooms) acting upon human chromosomes derived from peripheral blood lymphocytes. Doses 10 times those obtained in addicted (or even intoxicated) persons inhibited cell proliferation although lymphoblastogenesis was observed. Structural alterations observed with lower doses of the drug seen in chromosomes, showed a statistical difference with those observed in the control group.
