2283. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6097094
T1  - Catecholamines and schizophrenia
T3  - SCHIZOPHRENIE ET CATECHOLAMINES
A1  - Chouinard G. 
Y1  - 1975//
N2  - Schizophrenia is a major problem for public health. The present treatment of schizophrenia is symptomatic and non curative. A fairly high percentage of schizophrenic patients do not respond to conventional treatment. Amphetamine psychosis could serve as a model of schizophrenia. The importance of catecholamine metabolism in schizophrenia is based on the following facts: drugs that induce or provoke schizophrenia increase the action of the cerebral catecholamines; on the other hand, all antipsychotic drugs decrease or interfere with the brain catecholamines; recent studies indicate a possible increase of the activity of catecholamine in schizophrenic patients.
