2301. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6027087
T1  - Preferred conformations of serotonin in relation to receptor sites
A1  - Kumbar M.
A1  - Sankar D.V.S. 
Y1  - 1975//
N2  - Using an empirical method, 3 preferred conformations for serotonin are predicted. These 3 conformations corresponding to 1 extended form (phi=80degree, psi=180degree), and two folded forms (phi=280degree, and psi=100degree, phi=100degree, psi=290degree). The calculated intramolecular distances in both forms agree with those obtained by the X ray crystallography of various indoleamines. Furthermore, the dual receptor binding activity of serotonin is explained in terms of extended and folded conformations.
