2302. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6005507
T1  - Non delirious toxic psychoses in children
T3  - NICHTDELIRANTE INTOXIKATIONSPSYCHOSEN IM KINDESALTER
A1  - Eggers C. 
Y1  - 1975//
N2  - Six children are described with acute and reversible toxic psychoses whose (mainly visual) hallucinations together with conditions of excitation and hyperactivity were the most striking features of the psychopathological picture. In contrast to the more frequent delirious confusion (delirium) disturbances of consiciousness and orientation were missing. The phenomenological characteristics of hallucinosis in children (a condition so far not specified in the case of infants and children) have been elaborated with regard to other psychotic phenomena during infancy and adult age. Relevant neurophysiological and psychodevelopmental findings are reported.
