2306. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 5026944
T1  - Amines in schizophrenia
A1  - Snyder S.H.
A1  - Banerjee S.P. 
Y1  - 1974//
N2  - Some drug actions suggest a role for dopamine; others implicate the indoleamines. The 'dopamine story' derives from the influences of antischizophrenic phenothiazines and butyrophenones upon the synaptic activities of dopamine and studies of amphetamine psychosis as a model schizophrenia mediated via brain dopamine. Aspects of indoleamines relevant to schizophrenia are: the psychotomimetic actions of indoleamine related psychedelic drugs, and the existence of enzymes capable of methylating indoleamines to form psychedelic drugs in the human body.
