2322. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 5021677
T1  - The effects of psilocybin on EEG and behaviour in monkeys
A1  - Horibe M. 
Y1  - 1974//
N2  - Some 20 to 40 min after i.p. injections of psilocybin, 2 mg/kg, the monkeys' dynamic behavior increased, and in the neocortical EEG there was decreased alpha activity and enhanced beta activity. Between 1.5 and 3 hr after injection the animals became drowsy, and their neocortical EEG's showed high voltage slow waves and spindles: however the limbic EEG was still of characteristic alert pattern.
