2323. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 5181265
T1  - Psychodisleptic effects of Cannabis sativa
T3  - EFECTOS PSICODISLEPTICOS DE LA CANNABIS
A1  - Carranza Acevedo J. 
Y1  - 1974//
N2  - The pharmacological effects of cannabis in the human are reviewed, distinguishing its consistent psycho dysleptic action in hallucinatory psychotic states with acute administration and the mystico religious confusional states associated with its chronic administration. The psycho dysleptic effects of cannabis are contrasted with those of LSD-25, mescaline, psylocibine, Ditran and the amphetamines. The pharmacological activities of each of these substances is discussed. The large number of variables which must be taken into account to explain the individual differences in the effects of cannabis are described, and it is argued that this is one of the explanations which have arisen in the past regarding the cerebral actions of marijuana. Clinical data are presented regarding the amotivational syndrome of the chronic addict, and its reversibility is considered.
