2324. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 5181263
T1  - Brain damage and marijuana
T3  - DANO CEREBRAL Y MARIGUANA
A1  - Carranza Acevedo J. 
Y1  - 1974//
N2  - The concept of cerebral damage is defined with the observation that serious functional impairment of this organ may exist in the absence of detectable histologic lesions. It is emphasized that marijuana is a mixture of active substances in highly variable proportions so that its action is unpredictable if its chemical composition is not taken into account. Factors determining these variations are mentioned. The compound 9 delta tetrahydrocannabinol is defined as a psychodysleptic and as such is compared with other psychomimetics. Information on organic damage detected by changes in the Bender test and radiographic data of cerebral atrophy in chronic addicts are presented.
