TY  - JOUR
ID  - 6167235
T1  - Pathophysiology of experimental psychosis
A1  - Kolarik J. 
Y1  - 1974//
N2  - The present paper deals with EEG analysis of two main representatives of psychotomimetic substances: tryptamine psychotomimetics modelled on the effect of psilocybin (Ps) and anticholinergic psychotomimetics modelled on the effect of scopolamine. Analyzing the results obtained, we tried to define the involved structures of the CNS. The comparison of both groups of psychotomimetic substances and their effect on the EEG pattern served us to point out general features of experimental psychosis.
