2350. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 4091025
T1  - Induction and extinction of psilocybin induced transformations of visual space
A1  - Hill R.M.
A1  - Fischer R. 
Y1  - 1973//
N2  - There is a 'natural' tendency to misjudge the position of the visual as compared to the gravitational vertical. A 160 mug/kg psilocybin induced accentuation of this misjudgment in 16 college age volunteers, and a further augmentation in their accentuated drug response after exposure to strong body distortion is reported. Both types of drug effects, i.e. the accentuation as well as its augmentation, can be temporarily extinguished by sudden removal of the strong body distortion.
