2353. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 4067409
T1  - The effects of LSD, psilocybin, harmaline and amphetamine on the body temperature of para chlorophenylalanine pretreated rats
A1  - Ladefoged O. 
Y1  - 1973//
N2  - The effects of four psychopharmacologically active compounds on the rectal temperature were examined in both untreated and para chlorophenylalanine (pCPA) pretreated normal and febrile rats. The hyperthermic effect of amphetamine was reduced in both normal and febrile animals after pCPA pretreatment. Harmaline, psilocybin and LSD caused hypothermia in the rat. pCPA pretreatment antagonized the effect of harmaline but potentiated the effects of LSD and psilocybin. The same effect of pCPA pretreatment was seen in both the normal and the febrile animals.
