2564. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 293047470
T1  - Psilocybin
A1  - Mulkey D. 
Y1  - 1972//
N2  - Psilocybin is a naturally occurring indole alkylamine found in various species of new world mushrooms. It enjoyed widespread use among the pre Columbian cultures of Central America and has recently found its way into the present youth drug culture. The pharmacologic properties and physiologic effects of psilocybin are similar to those of LSD 25 as are the psychologic changes induced by the ingestion of the drug. The primary differences between psilocybin and LSD 25 are those of duration of action and potency. Details of the biochemistry, physiologic effects and metabolism as well as history of social usage and legal status of psilocybin are discussed.
