T1  - II. The effects of some hallucinogens on aggressiveness of mice and rats
A1  - Kostowski W.
A1  - Rewerski W.
A1  - Piechocki T. 
Y1  - 1972//
N2  - The action of 1 methylpiperid 3 yl benzilate (JB 336), psilocybin, ibogaine and bufotenine on the aggressiveness of isolated mice, and on the muricide reaction of rats, was investigated. All drugs produced a substantial decrease in aggressiveness, but this effect was dependent on isolation time, time after injection and the type of test used.
