2568. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 293147295
T1  - Psychedelic drugs: A thrent to reproduction?
A1  - Berlin C.M.
A1  - Jacobson C.B. 
Y1  - 1972//
N2  - Substantial numbers of young adults in the reproductive age group are being exposed to drugs and chemicals (chiefly illicit) for the purpose of altering mood, thought, or perception. These compounds have received little or no testing in any biological system. Since the source may involve attempts at amateur synthesis, contamination (usually by organic solvents) is quite likely. The structure of many of the compounds involved suggests that they may alter the structure or function, or both, of DNA. Laboratory or animal studies have supported this hypothesis; human data, particularly the chromosomal data, are in conflict Individual variations in drug metabolism may determine those subjects in whom potentially dangerous chemicals are formed in vivo from ingested psychedelic drugs.
