2585. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 289072049
T1  - A study of the role of noradrenaline in behavioural changes produced in the rat by psychotomimetic drugs
A1  - Sugrue M.F. 
Y1  - 1969//
N2  - LSD 25, psilocybin and JB 329 reduced the noradrenaline content of the rat hypothalamus. All 3 drugs affected the acquisition of a conditioned avoidance response, LSD 25 and psilocybin retarding and JB 329 enhancing the acquisition. With the exception of JB 329, doses affecting the acquisition of a conditioned avoidance response were lower than those required to decide hypothalamic noradrenaline concentrations. The time of peak drug effect on the acquisition of a conditioned avoidance response occurred approximately 1.5 hr after injection as opposed to 3 hr in the case of noradrenaline content The amount of LSD 25, psilocybin and JB 329 necessary to elicit gross behavioral excitation was similar to the dose producing noradrenaline depletion. Here also peak behavioral effect was detected earlier. Pretreatment with reserpine and alpha MT had no effect on the intensity of gross behavioral excitation induced by LSD 25 and psilocybin but shortened the duration of the response. The excitation induced by JB 329 was abolished by reserpine pretreatment and was markedly reduced both in intensity and duration by the prior injection of alpha MT.
