T1  - The influence of personality structure on the final result of model psychoses
T3  - DER EINFLUSS der STRUKTUR der PERSONLICHKEIT auf den AUSGANG der MODELLPSYCHOSE
A1  - Hockey M.A. 
Y1  - 1969//
N2  - With psylocybin an experimental psychotic condition could be induced in 15 volunteers and evaluated by the Minnesota Multiphasic Personality Inventory (MMPI), among which also the 2 reaction types occurred called exogenous and endogenous by Bonhoeffer's terminology. The degree of retest variability in the taste threshold value without any drug depends on the personality structure. The individual personality structure decisively determines reaction form, intensity, and final result of the psychosis.
