T1  - Hallucination of geometric forms associated with the use of sympatho mimetic agents
A1  - Kane Jr. F.J.
A1  - Keeler M.H.
A1  - Liptzin M.B.
A1  - Reifler C.B. 
Y1  - 1969//
N2  - Three cases of acute paranoid psychosis with hallucination of colored geometric forms are reported associated with the use of sympathomimetic agents. No signs of organicity were present in these cases. These phenomena probably reflect alterations in neuronal activity in the retina as a result of the presence of central adrenergic stimulation. These phenomena have also been reported with other central adrenergic stimulants notably lysergide, psilocybine and mescaline.
