T1  - Psychedelic effect of pholiota spectabilis
A1  - Buck R.W. 
Y1  - 1967//
N2  - P. spectabilis (Gymnopilus spectabilis) is a wellknown and recognizable wild mushroom that is generally considered inedible only because of its bitter taste, although attention has recently been called to it s hallucinogenic properties. Thin-layer chromatography of a methanol extract indicated the presence of indole derivatives, but there was no probable evidence of the presence of psilocinof psilocybin. (2C1 8B*).
