2605. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 287076036
T1  - Effects of mescaltne and psilocybin on dominance behavior of the rat
A1  - Uyeno E.T. 
Y1  - 1967//
N2  - Two dose-response experiments indicated that mescaline and psilocybin inhibited dominance behavior of rats competing for food. The times of peak inhibitory effects of mescaline and psilocybin are 30 min after the i. p. injection. The dose-response curves show that per cent inhibition of dominance behavior is an increasing function of dose. The ED of the mescaline curve is 4.02 mg/kg (3.14-5.15 mg/kg), and that of the psilocybin curve is 0.215 mg/kg (0.159-0.290 mg/kg).
