2608. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 287107121
T1  - Effect of certain psychopharmacologic substances on S35-methionine cytoplasm incorporation (cyrillic)
A1  - Petkov V.
A1  - Shoumkov G.
A1  - Koushev V. 
Y1  - 1966//
N2  - The effect of certain psychopharmacologic substances on S35-methionine cytoplasmic incorporation was studied by autohistoradiographic technics. It was shown that the psychanaleptic methylphenidate increased incorporation of S35-methionine in the cytoplasm of the brain and liver cells (tests on rats) while the neuroleptic chlorpromazine decreased it. Centrophenoxine decreases the incorporation of labeled methionine in the cytoplasm of the liver cells (tests on mice). Serotonin also decreased the incorporation of S35-methionine in the liver cells and increased it in the cells of the renal convoluted tubules. The antiserotonin methysergide increased incorporation of S35-methionine in the cytoplasm of all organs tested (liver, spleen and kidney), while under the effect of the antiserotonin psilocybine this increase was observed only in the cytoplasm of the liver cells. The combined application of serotonin with methysergide or with psilocybine resulted in considerable balancing of the effect achieved by the isolated application of each of the substances in the incorporation of the marked amino acid (tests on mice).
