T1  - Eeg effects of psychoanaleptics and biogenic amine precursors in reserpinized rabbits
T3  - Modification de l'EEG du Lapin re se r pine par les psychoanaleptiques et les precurseurs d'aminee biege nes
A1  - Kakajirna H.
A1  - Thuillier J. 
Y1  - 1966//
N2  - Different antidepressant substances do not all have the same effect on rabbit EEG. While imipramine and serotonin produce analogous and psilocybin similar changes in the EEG1 mefexamide and TOPA do not cause any anomalies at all. The possible relationship of these anomalies to tryptaminergic effects, which are found in certain antidepressants and not in others, is discussed. (IIC, 8a).
