2611. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 287073834
T1  - The LSD-controversy
T3  - De LSD-controverse
A1  - Brocker R.F.J. 
Y1  - 1966//
N2  - As a result of press and television publicity, psycholytics have been increasingly brought to the attention of the general public both at home and abroad. In a letter to the Editor of this journal, Sandoz have announced that they only supply LSD and psilocybin to psychiatrists in exceptional cases. After a brief survey of scientific research in this field, the therapeutic and religious speculations which have given rise to a serious controversy among psychiatrists on the advantages and disadvantages of psycholytic therapy are discussed. Two cases treated with LSD are reported. A hypothesis on the psychologic effect of these drugs is framed, which may also serve to elucidate the possible backgrounds of this dispute.
