2612. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281498076
T1  - The effects of tryptamine and alpha-methyl-tryptamine on the general and coronary haemodynamics and metabolism of the dog
A1  - Maxwell G.M. 
Y1  - 1965//
N2  - Cardiac output (Fick), and coronary flow (N2O Fick) were measured before and after infusion of tryptamine or a- methyltryptamine. Both drugs were found to increase cardiac output, and systemic and pulmonary arterial mean blood pressures. Coronary flow also increased, and, with tryptamine, an increase in coronary sinus oxygen content was recorded. Some of the properties of serotonin, or-methyltryptamine, and psilocybin are also present in the simpler compound tryptamine. (IIC, 18).
