2617. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 286095794
T1  - The effects of psilocybin on a test of after-image perception
A1  - Keeler M.H. 
Y1  - 1965//
N2  - After-image perception is measured by competition of a colored light with white light of different intensity. A list of spontaneous visual responses is answered by the participants in the trial. In double blind experiments either 2 mg. per kg. of psilocybin or a placebo was given orally. Correlation between results after psilocybin of the 2 series is 0.88 (p<0.001). A tentative hypothesis is offered that a relative decrease in inhibitory as compared to excitatory reactivity in cone-based processes might favor the imagery of visions.
