2620. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281547491
T1  - On janet's psychasthenia
T3  - O Janetove psychastenii
A1  - Dosuzkov Th. 
Y1  - 1964//
N2  - Janet's description of psychasthenia lacks a basic syndrome, a clinical course of the disorder and its pathogenetic mechanisms. It is no more than a group of symptoms which Janet did not consider hysterical and may also be present in other neuroses and psychoses (except paranoia). The notion of psychasthenia as a clinical, and even more so as a nosological entity is rejected. It is assumed to be a variety of psychopathy and schizophrenia.
