T1  - 'Model psychosis' produced by inhalation of gasoline fumes
A1  - Tolan E.J.
A1  - Lingl F.A. 
Y1  - 1964//
N2  - Two teen-age cases of toxic psychosis associated with gasoline inhalation are described and compared with the so-called 'model psychoses' evoked by mescaline. LSD -25 and psilocybin. The symptoms were predominantly autonomic, perceptual and affective. The perceptual experiences included mucn personally significant symbolic content. The inhaling of gasoline quickly became a tempting recurrent activity in the case of these two boys with maladjusted and impulsive personalities.
