2629. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281494012
T1  - Clinical experiences with the new psychodrug psilocybin
T3  - Nasa klinicka iskustva sa novim psihofarmakom psilocybin-om
A1  - Dordevic D. 
Y1  - 1964//
N2  - The drug was administered subcutaneously to a group of 30 hospitalized neurotics, in doses of 3-6 mg., 2 to 4 times a day. Considerable clinical improvement was seen in 53% of all patients treated, especially in acute depressive neurotic reactions. Owing to its ability to recall to consciousness forgotten and unpleasant experiences and conflicts, and to its euphoric effect, psilocybin is an excellent adjuvant in psychotherapeutic procedures. The individual reaction to psilocybin varies. It depends on the intellect of the patient and on his readiness to elaborate on the material that he has re-experienced. The patient does not develop tolerance to the drug, nor have addiction or complications been encountered.
