2640. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281546068
T1  - Auto-observation of two experimental intoxications with psilocybin
T3  - Auto-observation de deux intoxications experimentales par la Psilocybine
A1  - Wiart Cl. 
Y1  - 1963//
N2  - A report of 2 oral auto-intoxications with 10 mg. of psilocybin. The first test with 2 observers present, aimed unsuccessfully at painting the visual phenomena. The second test was undertaken to obtain a better understanding of the problems of delirium. The tests were made at intervale of 2 months. The pertinent experiences, which are fundamentally different,are not described in their chronological appearance but as perceived and experienced phenomena (illusions, hallucinoses and hallucinations of the various sensory organs). These are then grouped as regards their formation and interconnection with the multiple influences of external reality, somatic modification, ideo-affectivity, and personality. An attempt is made to determine the level of consciousness of the intoxicated individual and to indicate the elements of belief which through the mediation of irrefutable certainty and a truly fertile moment bring about genuine, primary delirious experiences.
