A1  - Gandiglio G.
A1  - Vercellino F. 
Y1  - 1962//
N2  - The authors conducted 2 experiments to investigate the effects of psylocibine. The first concerned 5 chronic schizophrenics and 5 cases of affective depressive psychosis. Each was given 2 mg. and 8 mg. of the drug by mouth for 10 days. In the second a normally healthy volunteer and 10 patients suffering from various mental diseases were given 3 mg. of the drug by the i.v. route. Some EEG changes were observed in the second group. It is concluded that psylocibine may be of therapeutic value in some selected cases, and may be used for revealing psychopathological structures and some aspects of the patient's individuality.
