2650. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281222283
T1  - Cross tolerance between mescaline and LSD-25 with a comparison of the mescaline and LSD reactions
A1  - Wolbach Jr. A.B.
A1  - Isbell H.
A1  - Miner E.J. 
Y1  - 1962//
N2  - Reactions caused by i. m. administration of 0.75 mug./kg. and 1.5 mug./kg. of lysergide (LSD) were compared with those caused by mescaline (2.5 and 5.0 mg./kg.) in the same 10 subjects. Both drugs caused pupil dilatation, rise of temperature, pulse rate and systolic blood pressure, and lowering of threshold for elicitation of the knee-jerk. Similar abnormal mental states (anxiety, difficulty in thinking, mood changes - generally euphoric, altered sensory perception - particularly visual, and alterations of body image) were reported by the subjects after both drugs. Effects of mescaline appeared more slowly and persisted somewhat longer than those of lysergide. Weight for weight, lysergide tartrate is 2400-4900 times as potent as mescaline; on a molecular basis lysergide is 4500-9275 times as potent as mescaline. Patients receiving lysergide daily developed direct tolerance to lysergide and were also cross-tolerant to mescaline, and vice versa. It is inferred that lysergide,psilocybin and mescaline probably share common mechanisms of action or some common final pathway.
