2651. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281221861
T1  - Effects of LSD-25, psilocybin and psilocin on temporal lobe EEG patterns and learned behavior in the cat
A1  - Adey W.R.
A1  - Bell F.R.
A1  - Dennis B.J. 
Y1  - 1962//
N2  - The effects of LSD-25, psilocybin and psilocin were studied in 18 cats with electrodes chronically implanted in the amygdala, parts of the hippocampus and entorhinal cortex, the anterior ventral thalamus, rostral midbrain reticular formation and the primary visual cortex. Electrical seizure-like activity was seen which was in part dependent on dosage but probably had its maximal effect in the dorsal hipocampus and entorhinal cortex; the seizures seemed to be critically dependent on the reduction of visual and auditory sensory influence but were frequently associated with the ingestion of food. Tolerance to LSD appeared when doses were repeated at intervals more frequent than 7-10 days. Psilocybin and psilocin had the same general effects as LSD-25.
