N2  - When introduced extracellularly by an electrophoretic technique into the lateral geniculate body the following substances (in descending order of activity) reversibly inhibited orthodromic impulses but not antidromic impulses: serotonin, tryptamine, bufotenin, lysergide, psilocin, psilocybin, 3-hydroxytyramine, noradrenaline, adrenaline and bromolysergide. Creatinine and glutamic acid had no effect. Glutamic acid and psilocybin were introduced as anions at pH 8 and the other substances as cations at pH 4.
