2660. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281076336
T1  - Experiments with psilocybin, a psychotropic substance from psilocybe Mexicana
T3  - Untersuchungen mit psilocybin, einer psychotropen substanz aus psilocybe Mexicana
A1  - Rummele W.
A1  - Cnirss F. 
Y1  - 1961//
N2  - The reaction induced by a single dose of psilocybin has been observed in 18 trials, the drug having been administered orally and subcutaneously in an equal number of cases. A dose of 6 mg. of psilocybin proved to produce definite mental effects without severe physical disturbances. During a first phase of intoxication, activity was diminished; during the second phase, an increase in activity together with a prevailing euphoric, rarely dysphoric moodiness occurred. About half of the subjects reported an altered sensory perception, less often a feeling of depersonalization. With parenteral administration marked autonomic effects occurred, such as bradycardia, increased blood pressure, respiratory changes, diminution in respiratory rate and increase in respiratory volume, headache and vertigo. One of the cases given 10 mg. of psilocybin parenterally showed marked autonomic disturbance, elementary hallucinations and a feeling of depersonalization.
