2661. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281075834
T1  - Psilocybine - Its therapeutic aspects
T3  - La psilocybine. See implications therapeutiques
A1  - Delay J.
A1  - Pichot P.
A1  - Lemperiere T. 
Y1  - 1961//
N2  - A report is submitted of a clinical study in which psilocybine was used in oneiro-analysis. This study was carried out on 47 normal subjects and 90 mental patients; the substance was administered orally or by i. m. injections, in a dosage of 9-14 mg. The drug had a pronounced neuro-vegetative effect on normal subjects as well as on patients. Mydriasis, changes in the pulse and unstable blood pressure were commonly observed. The mental effects in normal subjects differed from those observed in the patients. Experimental intoxication with psilocybine caused a cycle of manifestations which lasted 4 hr., with a maximal intensity around the 2nd hr. The first sign was a change in mood and in activity; subsequently there appeared alterations of perception, illusions, visual hallucinations and disturbances of consciousness. In the mental patients, the drug intensified the manifestations of the psychosis or the underlying neurosis, so that they were easier to identify. The therapeutic effect of psilocybine was twofold: biological and psychological. The psychological effect was due to the utilization of the material provided during the attack, and to the modifications of the relationship between the physician and the patient.
