2662. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281075817
T1  - Auto-experiment with psilocybine
T3  - Onkiserlet psilocybinnel
A1  - Kiraly J. 
Y1  - 1961//
N2  - The pharmacopsychiatric effect of dimethyl- and diethyltryptamine and psilocybine was studied. The author consumed during the experiment 9 mg. psilocybine per os and observed subsequently vegetative symptoms, temporary writing troubles, tachycardia and strong tremor, hyperaesthesia of the sense of touch, euphoria, temporary dominance of the first signalling system, illusions and pseudohallucinations. Psilocybine produced synaesthetic experiences in a smaller degree than diethyltryptamine. These experiences were not diffused over the entire sensorial sphere as was the case with diethyltryptamine tests, and hypnagogic visions did not follow the rhythm of sound stimuli. During the entire experiment, self-control was always maintained. Vivid 'lilliput' visions and periodical troubles of consciousness explain the cultic practices of primitives who attribute a 'divinative', 'clairvoyant' effect to this drug.
