2664. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281359269
T1  - Clinical, biochemical and psychologic effects of psilocybin
A1  - Hollister L.E. 
Y1  - 1961//
N2  - Psilocybin was tested on 16 normal volunteers, 9 subjects receiving both oral (60-200 mug./kg.) and s. c. (37-203 mug./kg.) doses. Psilocybin has a shorter span of action than lysergide or mescaline, peak effects occurring between 90 and 120 min. after medication. It is more agreeable to subjects than lysergide and produces dreamy states without marked impairment of faculties. Pupillary dilatation and increased deep tendon reflexes were constantly observed. Inorganic phosphorus excretion and total eosinophils were reduced. In the psychomimetic field, psilocybin decreased motivation, but did not influence accuracy.
