N2  - Sensory attenuation, a modified form of sensory deprivation where sensory inputs are controlled, is described as a method useful for the study of drug responses. The above is a preliminary report about a comparative study, using this technique, of the following 3 psychotomimetic drugs: (1) sernyl 1, (1-phenylcyclohexyl)piperidine monohydrochloride (May and Baker C 1395); (2) psilocybin, a tryptamine derivative: isolated active principle of Psilocybe mexicana heim, a Mexican mushroom (Sandoz); (3) LSD-25, D-lysergic acid diethylamide (Sandoz).
