2669. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 281075808
T1  - The use of dysleptic substances in psychotherapy. Favourable results of repeated sessions
T3  - A propos de l'utilisation des substances dysleptiquee en psychotherapie. Resultats favorables de seances repetees
A1  - Stevenin L.
A1  - Benoit J.C. 
Y1  - 1960//
N2  - The use of psychodysleptic substances is suggested in individual psychotherapy of neurotics. A description is given of the use of psychodysleptics on the same patient, during 27 consecutive weekly sessions; the substances used were psilocybine (6 times), mescaline (11 times) and LSD (10 times). The 30-year-old patient had, at the end of his adolescence, exhibited symptoms of anxiety with a schizoid basis, character disorders and great difficulties in social adaptation. Although he partly benefited from psychoanalysis (classical Freudian method), he suffered from social and affective maladaptations, feelings of inferiority, insomnia (mild, without dreams) and myospasms. Dysleptic medication, particularly with mescaline, had an interesting effect. Progressive improvement was seen; his field of activity is greatly extended and his social conduct has become normalized.
