N2  - Dyflos (DFP), lysergide (LSD), bromolysergide, chlorpromazine, psilocybin. N,N-dimethyltryptamine, nalorphine, cocaine, harmine and the 2 -diethylaminoethyl ester hydrochloride of alpha-cyclopentyl-2-thiopheneglycolic acid ('WIN 2299') were found to exert varying inhibitory effects on typical human serum ChE. Differences in sensitivity of typical and atypical forms of human serum ChE to these agents are discussed. Plotnikoff - Menlo Park, Calif.
