2673. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 280632062
T1  - The new chemotherapy in psychiatry. Results and statistics
T3  - Lee nouvelles chimiotherapies en psychiatrie. Resultats et statistiques
A1  - Delay J. 
Y1  - 1959//
N2  - The results of the therapy of mental disorders in children during the last 7 yr. are given statistically. The medicaments are divided into 3 groups: psycholeptics, psychoanaleptics and psychodysleptics. Among the newer psycholeptics, the so-called new neuroleptics are mentioned, including the group of chlor pro mazine and the Rauwolfia preparations. They induce the psycho motor syndrome. After the use of neuroleptics, the number of patients admitted diminished, and the excitative and restless states almost completely disappeared. They had a good influence in the maniacal, hypomaniacal and hallucinatory states, and also in schizophrenia. Psychoanaleptics were useful in the depressive and the melancholic states. Beside the different amines, derivatives of isonicotinic acid and iminodibenzyl (imipramine) are available. The author emphasizes the effectiveness of the combined therapy with imipramine and some of the neuroleptics, as for instance laevomepromazine. Among the psychodysleptics, the author mentions psilocybine, a hallucinogenic drug, whose formula resembles that of serotonin. It produces a dissolution of the mental synthesis, and a liberation of psychological automatism. The author's opinion is that this drug is useful in the new type of psychotherapy which is called chemical psychoanalysis. It is of great value in the therapy of the different neuroses.
