ID  - 280660441
T1  - Psilocybin, a psychotropic active substance from the mexican narcotic mushroom psilocybe mexicana heim
T3  - Psilocybin, ein psychotroper wirkstoff aus dem mexikanischen rauschpilz (psilocybe mexicana heim)
A1  - Hofmann A.
A1  - Hein R.
A1  - Brack A.
A1  - Kobel H. 
Y1  - 1958//
N2  - This Psilocybe species has been cultivated and the active component extracted from the fruit body and the sclerotium. Chromatographically, 2 fractions were separated and by further purification 2 different substances were obtained. The elementary composition of the first one, called psilocybin, is C13H18(20)O3N2P2. As a UV spectrum it shows the characteristics of an indole derivative with substitution on the benzene nucleus. The 2nd substance, psilocin, is very unstable and has not yet been analysed. An oral dose of 4-8 mg. of psilocybin produces in human subjects a state of hypnosis somewhat similar to that with mescaline and lasting several hours.
