2678. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 280662329
T1  - Pharmacology of psilocybin, a drug from psilocybe mexicana heim
T3  - Zur pharmakologie von psilocybin, einem wirkstoff aus psilocybe mexicana heim
A1  - Weidmann H.
A1  - Taeschler M.
A1  - Konzett H. 
Y1  - 1958//
N2  - Psilocybin does not produce any characteristic effects on isolated organs, but in the intact mouse it causes mydriasis and piloerection in doses of not less than 10 mg./kg. s.c. In the unanaesthetized rabbit a dose of 1 mg./kg. i.v. suffices to cause mydriasis, tachycardia, tachypnoea and rise of temperature. The picture as a whole is that of central sympathetic stimulation, although the depression of motor activity does not agree with this.
