2713. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 2017-43726-044
T1  - Nutraceutical and alternative treatments for obsessive-compulsive and related disorders.
T2  - Obsessive-compulsive disorder: Phenomenology, pathophysiology, and treatment.
A1  - Camfield, David A
A1  - Sarris, Jerome
A3  - Pittenger, Christopher [Ed]
Y1  - 2017//
N2  - This chapter reviews current research into nutraceutical substances that have been investigated in the treatment of OCD or of grooming disorders, through either case studies or open-label and/or randomized placebo-controlled trials with some evidence of efficacy. The substances to be considered are myo-inositol, St John's wort, milk thistle, borage, glycine, sarcosine, psilocybin, and A/-acetylcysteine. A description of each substance is presented, together with relevant biochemistry and interpretation regarding the current evidence of efficacy and safety/tolerability as well as what can be determined about factors which may moderate its efficacy including OCD symptom severity and advice in regards to concomitant antidepressant use. Conclusions and recommendations for future research are also presented. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
