2724. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 2017-48411-003
T1  - The resurgence of the clinical research with hallucinogens.
T2  - El resurgimiento de la investigacion clinica con alucinogenos.
A1  - Velder, Anja Loizaga
A1  - Trevino, Carlos Viesca
A2  - Alper, Bastiaans, Baumeister, Bogenschutz, Bogenschutz, Brown, Chabrol, Drewniany, Dutta, Fernandez, Frecska, Gable, Gasser, Gasser, Gasser, Glick, Grinspoon, Grob, Grob, Hendricks, Hermle, Johansen, Johnson, Johnson, Jungaberle, Krebs, Krupitsky, Krupitsky, Labate, Leuner, Leuner, Loizaga-Velder, Mabit, Mash, Mash, McGlothin, Mithoefer, Mithoefer, Mithoefer, Moreno, Moreno, Morris, Nichols, Nutt, Oehen, Oliveira-Lima, Osorio, Osorio, Palhano-Fontes, Passie, Sanches, Schenberg, Serafini, Sershen, Strassman, Strassman, Thomas, Tupper
Y1  - 2017//
N2  - Clinical research with hallucinogens is reemerging after an interruption in this line of research that lasted for several decades. In several universities around the world research is being conducted in clinical trials of psychotherapy assisted with: psilocybin, LSD, ayahuasca, 3,4-3,4- methylenedioxymethamphetamine (MDMA) and ketamine; for treatment indications that include: end of life anxiety related to terminal illnesses, substance dependency disorders, obsessive compulsive disorders, post traumatic stress disorder and depression. Preliminary studies indicate favorable therapeutic outcomes within reasonable safety margins in professional therapeutic contexts. This research indicates that adverse reactions associated with psychedelics are primarily a consequence of inappropriate use. Further controlled studies with larger number of participants are necessary, to adequately evaluate the therapeutic potential and risk of clinical application of these substances. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
Abstract (French)
La recherche clinique avec les hallucinogenes reapparait apres une interruption de cette ligne de recherche qui a duree plusieurs decennies. Dans universites renommees des essais cliniques de psychotherapie assistee par: psilocybine, LSD, ayahuasca, 3,4-methylenedioxymethamphetamine (MDMA) et ketamine sont menees, pour les indications de traitement qui incluent: anxiete des patientes qui souffrent de maladies terminales, dependance aux substances, troubles obsessionnels compulsifs, syndrome de stress post-traumatique et depression. Des etudes preliminaires indiquent les resultats therapeutiques favorables avec de marges de securite raisonnables dans les contextes therapeutiques professionnels. Cette recherche nous indique que les effets indesirables lies aux psychedeliques sont principalement une consequence d'un usage inapproprie. D'autres etudes controlees avec un plus grand nombre de participants sont necessaires pour evaluer adequatement le potentiel therapeutique, ainsi que les risques d'application clinique de ces substances. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
Abstract (Spanish)
La investigacion clinica con alucinogenos esta resurgiendo despues de una interrupcion de varias decadas. En universidades de renombre se estan llevando a cabo ensayos clinicos de psicoterapia asistida por psilocibina, dietilamida de acido lisergico (LSD), ayahuasca, 3,4-metilendioximetanfetamina (MDMA) y ketamina, para indicaciones que incluyan ansiedad en pacientes con enfermedades terminales, trastorno por dependencia de sustancias, trastorno obsesivo-compulsivo, trastorno por estres postraumatico y depresion. Estudios preliminares indican resultados terapeuticos favorables con margenes de seguridad adecuada en contextos terapeuticos profesionales; las reacciones adversas principalmente son consecuencia de un uso inapropiado. Son necesarios mas estudios controlados con mayor numero de participantes, para poder evaluar adecuadamente el potencial terapeutico y los riesgos de la aplicacion clinica de esas sustancias. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2017 APA, all rights reserved)
