T1  - Can psychedelic compounds play a part in drug dependence therapy?
T3  - Journal of Mental Science, The Asylum Journal, The Asylum Journal of Mental Science
A1  - Sessa, Ben
A1  - Johnson, Matthew W
A2  - Bogenschutz, Connock, Doblin, Dyck, Halpern, Harkins, Hendricks, Hickman, James, Krupitsky, MacLean, Miller, Reus, Sessa
Y1  - 2015//
N2  - After a 40-year hiatus there is now a revisiting of psychedelic drug therapy throughout psychiatry, with studies examining the drugs psilocybin, ketamine, ibogaine and ayahuasca in the treatment of drug dependence. Limitations to these therapies are both clinical and legal, but the possibility of improving outcomes for patients with substance dependency imposes an obligation to research this area. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
