A1  - Schifano, F
AI  - ORCID: http://orcid.org/Arnone, D.; ORCID: http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3831-2301
A2  - Azmitia, Cowan, Daumann, Daumann, Jacobsen, Reneman, Ricaurte, Ricaurte, Sessa
Y1  - 2006//
N2  - Comments on the editorial by B. Sessa (see record 2005-06568-003) entitled "Can psychedelics have a role in psychiatry once again?" (Sessa, 2005) in which Dr. Sessa offers a detailed historical and heuristic perspective of psychedelics, with particular reference to psychotherapy. Reading the article the feeling was of sensed (by the author) repulsion of the 'neurobiological psychiatrist in relation to 'research that explores alternative states of consciousness', 'psychedelics research' as a 'viable neurobiologial substrate for the very human experience of religious encounter' and generally a possible use of psychedelics in psychiatry. We would like to discuss recent neurobiological findings related to one of the psychedelics mentioned by Dr. Sessa, which perhaps would offer an explanation as to why these substances have limited scope in psychiatry today. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
