2928. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 2007-11123-000
T1  - Psychedelic medicine: New evidence for hallucinogenic substances as treatments.
T2  - Psychedelic medicine: New evidence for hallucinogenic substances as treatments.
A1  - Winkelman, Michael J [Ed]
A1  - Roberts, Thomas B [Ed]
Y1  - 2007//
N2  - Psychedelic substances present in nature have been used by humans across hundreds of years to produce mind-altering changes in thought, mood, and perception--changes we do not experience otherwise except rarely in dreams, religious exaltation, or psychosis. In these groundbreaking volumes, top researchers explain the testing and research underway to use--under the guidance of a trained provider--psychedelic substances for better physical and mental health. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
In this, the second of a two volume set, we see that psychedelics are fulfilling the expectations of Valentina Pavlovna Wasson and R. Gordon Wasson as treatments for alcoholism and addiction (Part I: Treating Substance Abuse). "Part II: Guidelines for Psychotherapeutic Applications" shows us the progress since she recognized psychedelics as a likely treatment for mental diseases. Part III circles us back to the Wassons' original mystical and transpersonal adventures. Half a century later, the contributors to Part III pick up the Wassons' spiritual trail by recognizing that psychological growth pursued far enough becomes spiritual growth. As psychedelic mushrooms beckoned the Wassons 50 years ago, mushrooms and other psychedelics beckon us today to the transpersonal quest. The authors in this volume are our trail guides in medicine, psychotherapy, and positive psychology. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
