2959. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 2003-01549-020
DO  - http://dx.doi.org/10.1038/sj.npp.1300005
T1  - Effects of the 5-HT2A agonist psilocybin on mismatch negativity generation and AX-continuous performance task: Implications for the neuropharmacology of cognitive deficits in schizophrenia.
A1  - Umbricht, Daniel
A1  - Vollenweider, Franz X
A1  - Schmid, Liselotte
A1  - Grubel, Claudia
A1  - Skrabo, Anja
A1  - Huber, Theo
A1  - Koller, Rene
A2  - Adams, Aghajanian, Aghajanian, Aghajanian, Alain, Alain, Alho, Anand, Arvanov, Barch, Bilder, Bilder, Bilder, Breier, Buchsbaum, Catts, Chapman, Cohen, Cornblatt, Dehaene-Lambertz, Farber, Ford, Frodl-Bauch, Geyer, Gottfries, Gouzoulis-Mayfrank, Green, Green, Hasler, Hegerl, Hegerl, Hegerl, Hegerl, Hirayasu, Jaaskealainen, Jaaskealainen, Jaaskealainen, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Javitt, Juckel, Juckel, Kegeles, Korzyukov, Kreitschmann-Andermahr, Kreitschmann-Andermahr, Krystal, Landau, Lu, Lucas, Lucas, McKenna, Meltzer, Moghaddam, Moghaddam, Naatanen, Naatanen, Naatanen, Naatanen, Naatanen, Naatanen, Naatanen, Novak, Oades, Pang, Pantelis, Park, Perris, Purdon, Rabinowicz, Ritter, Roth, Saykin, Schall, Schooler, Schr, Servan-Schreiber, Shelley, Shutara, Snodgrass, Stip, Strous, Takahata, Teng, Tewes, Tiitinen, Tuchtenhagen, Umbricht, Umbricht, Umbricht, Vollenweider, Vollenweider, Vollenweider, Vollenweider, Vollenweider, von Knorring, Wang, Wexler, Wittchen, Woerner, Yan
Y1  - 2003//
N1  - Annual Convention of the Society of Biological Psychiatry. 54th. May, 1999. Washington. DC, US. The results of this study were presented in part at the aforementioned conference.
N2  - Previously the NMDA (N-methyl-D-aspartate) receptor (NMDAR) antagonist ketamine was shown to disrupt generation of the auditory event-related potential (FRP) mismatch negativity (MMN) and the performance of an AX-type continuous performance test (AX-CPT)--measures of auditory and visual context-dependent information processing--in a similar manner as observed in schizophrenia. This placebo-controlled study investigated effects of the 5-HT2A receptor agonist psilocybin on the same measures in 18 healthy volunteers (10 men, 8 women; mean age 25.1 yrs). Psilocybin administration induced significant performance deficits in the AX-CPT, but failed to reduce MMN generation significantly. These results indirectly support evidence that deficient MMN generation in schizophrenia may be a relatively distinct manifestation of deficient NMDAR functioning. In contrast, secondary pharmacological effects shared by NMDAR antagonists and the 5-HT2A agonist (i.e., disruption of glutamatergic neurotransmission) may be the mechanism underlying impairments in AX-CPT performance observed during both psilocybin and ketamine administration. Comparable deficits in schizophrenia may result from independent dysfunctions of 5-HT2A and NMDAR-related neurotransmission. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
