T1  - Increased activation of indirect semantic associations under psilocybin.
A1  - Spitzer, Manfred
A1  - Thimm, Markus
A1  - Hermle, Leo
A1  - Holzmann, Petra
A1  - Kovar, Karl-Artur
A1  - Heimann, Hans
A1  - Gouzoulis-Mayfrank, Euphrosyne
A1  - Kischka, Udo
A1  - Schneider, Frank
AI  - ORCID: http://orcid.org/Schneider, Frank; ORCID: http://orcid.org/0000-0003-1557-7956
Y1  - 1996//
N2  - Hypothesized that psilocybin might exert a defocusing effect on semantic networks (i.e., decrease the signal-to-noise ratio), which should lead to an increased indirect semantic priming effect. A double-blind, placebo-controlled study was conducted on the effects of psilocybin on semantic and indirect semantic priming with 8 normal males (mean age 39.4 yrs). The finding that psilocybin increases indirect semantic priming in normal Ss adds to the general understanding of the effects of hallucinogenic agents on cognitive functions. Data indicate that indirect semantic priming is a highly sensitive measure that appears to respond not only to pharmacologic intervention, but also to the psychological effects of the setting. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2018 APA, all rights reserved)
