N2  - This chapter examines the patterns of use, pharmacology, and biobehavioral consequences of the use and abuse of cannabis and hallucinogens. The chapter discusses the following topics: cannabis (absorption and metabolism; neuropharmacology; preparations, dosage, and routes of administration; acute effects; tolerance, withdrawal, and dependence; adverse effects on health, safety, and adjustment) and hallucinogens (acute effects; neuropharmacology, dosage, preparations, absorption, and metabolism; LSD; psilocybin, dimethyltriptamine; mescaline; designer drugs; PCP; ketamine; amanita muscaria; anticholinergic hallucinogens; tolerance, withdrawal, and dependence; adverse effects on health, safety, and adjustment). (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
