2979. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 1999-00365-009
DO  - http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/02791072.1998.10399716
T1  - Reflections on the Concord Prison Project and the follow-up study.
T3  - Journal of Psychedelic Drugs
A1  - Metzner, Ralph
Y1  - 1998//
N2  - Comments on the 34-yr follow-up study of the Concord Prison Project by R. Doblin (see record 1999-00365-008) in that T. Leary and the other researchers on the project, including the author, fell victim to the "halo effect" by which researchers tend to see their data in as positive light as possible. Doblin's analysis shows that most prisoners who were actually returned for parole violations had also committed new crimes; therefore, contradicting Leary's seemingly positive finding. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
