A1  - Gable, Robert S
Y1  - 1993//
N2  - Describes the author's personal experience of altered consciousness resulting from the ingestion of psilocybin mushrooms. This occurred when he was a graduate student 30 yrs prior, and the experience at the time was reported by the author to Maslow and Skinner. Their reactions to the report are briefly noted. The author suggests that his previous experience with hallucinogens has helped him communicate with terminally ill people who occasionally experience novel states of consciousness. This is illustrated in the account of a therapeutic interaction with a terminally ill hospice patient having a hallucinatory reaction to opiate medications. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
