2998. 
TY  - JOUR
ID  - 1992-20206-001
DO  - http://dx.doi.org/10.1080/02791072.1991.10472573
T1  - An ethnomycological review of psychoactive agarics in Australia and New Zealand.
T3  - Journal of Psychedelic Drugs
A1  - Allen, John W
A1  - Merlin, Mark D
A1  - Jansen, Karl L
Y1  - 1991//
N2  - Reviews the history of the accidental and purposeful use of psychoactive agarics in Australia and New Zealand (ANZ), using information reports in the scientific literature, news items, and personal communications with medical and law enforcement professionals. The chemical compounds and mycological identification of the mind-altering mushrooms known to have been ingested in ANZ are also discussed. The legal aspects involving their use in ANZ have been investigated and are described. 30 case studies provide a description and analysis of the medical and psychological results of both the accidental and deliberate ingestion of these psychoactive agarics that occurred during the past 50 yrs. Reports published over the past 30 yrs indicate that numerous species of mushrooms containing psilocybin and psilocin are being consumed in ANZ. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
